// MIRROR — the deployed source of truth is `Admin Auth Screen/storage.rules`
// (only that project has a `.firebaserc`, so `firebase deploy` runs from
// there). Keep both files byte-identical below this header; edit the admin one
// first.
//
// Firebase Storage is RETIRED in this project. This file is the honest record
// of that state, not an upload surface:
//   • Proposal photos and meal photos go to Cloudinary (Unsigned Direct
//     Upload); no code path in the mobile app or the admin panel writes here.
//   • The `firebase_storage` package is gone from this app's pubspec, and the
//     admin panel never imported it either — so nothing in shipped code can
//     even reach this bucket.
//
// Every write is therefore closed unconditionally. One piece of history is
// worth keeping: the deployed rules used to grant
// `allow write: if request.auth != null` on /meal_images, and because the
// mobile app signs in anonymously the moment a meal is proposed, that rule let
// any device on any network write unlimited, arbitrary-type objects into the
// bucket.
//
// Reads stay open on exactly the two legacy prefixes below, and deliberately:
// rows seeded before the Cloudinary move still carry /meal_images/... or
// /staging_meal_images/<uid>/... URLs in their `imageUrl` field, and closing
// those reads would not protect anything — it would only blank the photos of
// existing data. Newly written rows never reference Storage.
//
// `/staging_meal_images/{uid}/{fileName}` is NOT dead code even though the app
// stopped uploading to it: the admin dashboard still renders the stored
// `imageUrl` of pending proposals (Admin Auth Screen →
// admin_dashboard_screen.dart, staging triage list and dialog), and pending
// documents created before the Cloudinary move point at this path. Delete this
// block only once those legacy rows are purged or their URLs rewritten to
// Cloudinary — until then it is a read-only tombstone.
rules_version = '2';
service firebase.storage {
  match /b/{bucket}/o {
    // Legacy, read-only: meal photos seeded before the Cloudinary move.
    match /meal_images/{fileName} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow write: if false;
    }
    // Legacy, read-only: staging ("proposal") photos seeded before the
    // Cloudinary move — still displayed by the admin panel. See header.
    match /staging_meal_images/{uid}/{fileName} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow write: if false;
    }
    // Anything else in the bucket is unreachable in both directions.
    match /{allPaths=**} {
      allow read, write: if false;
    }
  }
}
